From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:36:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Describe the M4 driver as it is now

The help text still called the driver a development port of the Python
firmware shim. Say what it drives and what it needs from the bootloader.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/Kconfig | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/Kconfig
index 6d61de97a677..641170e59136 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/Kconfig
@@ -10,7 +10,9 @@ config DRM_ASAHI_M4
 	select RUST_APPLE_RTKIT
 	select APPLE_MAILBOX
 	help
-	  Rust DRM driver for the T8132 (M4) GPU, following the Asahi UAPI
-	  and the M4 Python DRM-shim firmware implementation. Intended for
-	  development under m1n1. Normal initialization is the default;
-	  probe_only selects identification without firmware startup.
+	  DRM driver for the GPU in Apple's M4 (T8132), with the Asahi UAPI
+	  Mesa's asahi drivers use. It needs m1n1 to hand the GPU over:
+	  its firmware, memory regions and calibration.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
+	  will be called asahi_m4.
